================================================================================
Third-party content and attribution
================================================================================

Fluency learns by *distillation* from external teacher models. No third-party
binary, kernel, runtime, or source code is embedded in Fluency — only learned
weights derived through Zig training code from sequences produced by
permissively-licensed teachers (Constitution, Article I.5 / III).

The following teacher models have been used as oracles during distillation
runs published with this repository. Their licenses permit derivative training
and the resulting Fluency weights are an original work of this project.

1. SmolLM2-360M-Instruct
   - Source: HuggingFaceTB / SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-GGUF (Q8_0 quantization)
   - Architecture: llama (32 layers, embd=960, vocab=49152)
   - License: Apache License 2.0
   - Used as: seq-KD teacher for the Fluency-139M overnight/smoke runs.

2. TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat
   - Source: TheBloke / TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0-GGUF (Q4_K_M quantization)
   - Architecture: llama (22 layers, embd=2048, vocab=32000)
   - License: Apache License 2.0
   - Used as: early pilot teacher (now superseded by SmolLM2 to fit memory
     budget on developer hardware).

